AdaptiveCpp 25.10.0 Level Zero event dependency lifetime correction.

Retain each submitted operation's wait events until that operation completes.
A predecessor can finish before its consumer has read the native wait handle;
replacing the queue's last event must not destroy that handle. Prepare ownership
before the asynchronous append, and wait before destroying the command list.

Level Zero requires events to outlive device references:
https://oneapi-src.github.io/level-zero-spec/level-zero/latest/core/api/apis/event.html#zeeventdestroy

Upstream source is BSD-2-Clause; retain its notices in the patched files.

